From 2713f5f6219d2959af7cac9b2ce23883375ab53d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Super User <root@localhost.localdomain>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 04:49:29 +0800
Subject: [09/12] KVM: arm64: Prevent HDBSS enable when dirty ring is active

HDBSS flushes dirty page entries via kvm_vcpu_mark_page_dirty() which
routes to the dirty bitmap path. Dirty ring mode uses a separate
buffer that is not populated by HDBSS hardware tracking, making the
two mechanisms incompatible. Refuse to enable HDBSS when dirty ring
is configured to prevent silent data loss during live migration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c
index 9ad027449498..3165a53b2944 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/dirty_bit.c
@@ -56,6 +56,9 @@ int kvm_arm_enable_hdbss_internal(struct kvm *kvm, unsigned int order)
 	if (order > HDBSS_MAX_SIZE)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (kvm->dirty_ring_size)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	if (kvm->arch.enable_hdbss)
 		return 0;
 
